        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Second solution. Choose a neighborhood N of 0 on which $g(x) \\neq 0$. Define the following functions on $N \\setminus \\{0\\}$: $h_1(x) = \\frac{f(x)g(x) - f(0)g(0)}{x}$; $h_2(x) = \\frac{f(x)g(0) - f(0)g(x)}{xg(0)g(x)}$; $h_3(x) = g(0)g(x)$; $h_4(x) = \\frac{1}{g(x) + g(0)}$. Then by assumption, $h_1, h_2, h_3, h_4$ all have limits as $x \\to 0$. On the other hand,",
          "block_bbox": [
            1410,
            676,
            2350,
            1000
          ],
          "block_id": 21,
          "block_order": 21,
          "group_id": 21,
          "block_polygon_points": [
