        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "B4 Number the games 1,..., 2011, and let  $ A = (a_{jk}) $ be the  $ 2011 \\times 2011 $ matrix whose jk entry is 1 if player k wins game j and  $ i = \\sqrt{-1} $ if player k loses game j. Then  $ \\overline{a_{hj}}a_{jk} $ is 1 if players h and k tie in game j; i if player h wins and player k loses in game j; and -i if h loses and k wins. It follows that  $ T + iW = \\overline{A}^{T}A $.",
          "block_bbox": [
            1351,
            1256,
            2350,
            1552
          ],
          "block_id": 24,
          "block_order": 24,
          "group_id": 24,
          "block_polygon_points": [
